why cargo_error_line constructs the owned paths Vec with exactly cwd and at most one target selected by rfind; the entire constructor is bound by the permanent proof control. Thus its length is one or two, so every position is first or last and both versions run the unchanged body in the same order. The rewrite counter advances at most twice; peek only moves a concrete PathBuf and invokes no user iterator or filesystem callback. Canonicalization and prefix insertion retain their ordering and values. Actual helper/trace variants cover absent/present targets, aliases, missing paths, relative targets and repeated values; same-edit wider Vec controls lose the middle and wrong positive/negative oracles fail. This source-cardinality argument, not those finite examples, establishes equivalence. Revalidate after constructor, type, iterator or body changes; no arbitrary-vector claim (leaf M3.6.9.6.3.2.2.14.3.2.2.2.1).

from-json "for spelling in std::iter::once(path).chain(canonical) {"
to-json "let mut __archogen_sweep_846_it = (std::iter::once(path).chain(canonical)).into_iter().peekable(); let mut __archogen_sweep_846_k = 0usize; while let Some(spelling) = __archogen_sweep_846_it.next() { let (__archogen_sweep_846_first, __archogen_sweep_846_last) = (__archogen_sweep_846_k == 0, __archogen_sweep_846_it.peek().is_none()); __archogen_sweep_846_k += 1; if !(__archogen_sweep_846_first || __archogen_sweep_846_last) { continue; }"
why cargo_error_line computes canonical as fs::canonicalize(&path).ok(), an Option<PathBuf>, before iterating std::iter::once(path).chain(canonical). This concrete chain has exactly one or two elements. Each is an end, so the actual ends rewrite visits every raw/canonical spelling in the same order and cannot overflow its at-most-two counter. Peeking moves the optional owned PathBuf without a filesystem call or user iterator callback; the unchanged ancestor/prefix body sees identical spellings. Permanent source-constructor guards, actual compiled helper/ordered traces and successful/missing canonical paths hold the premises; a wider Vec-backed chain compiles and loses its middle, and wrong wider/positive/negative oracles fail. Finite examples supplement the universal cardinality proof. Revalidate after constructor, type, iterator or body changes; no arbitrary-chain claim (leaf M3.6.9.6.3.2.2.14.3.2.2.2.1).

