why On supported Unix Cargo-built callers, cwd is absolute: inventory/baseline derive from Cargo's absolute manifest root, the repaired gate canonicalizes its repository before output joins, inventory joins out/tree, and compile is the sole production run_cargo caller. The helper retains absolute targets or joins relative targets to that cwd; raw/canonical ancestors, lossy conversion and apostrophe quoting preserve a leading slash. The unconditional guard adds only prefixes with no newline. Such a match cannot straddle a physical line start (byte zero or after newline), and at begin equality its slash disagrees with the candidate's error prefix. It therefore suppresses no additional candidate for any stderr/environment in this domain; returned bytes and empty result remain unchanged. This is a universal prefix/line-boundary proof, not finite-example inference. Permanent exact production/caller guards, actual compiled original/edit, literal and generated records, native Cargo root through relative manifest/alias, relative wider witnesses, altered-premise and wrong-oracle controls bind scope. Revalidate guarded source, callers/root/constructors, conversion, line framing or Unix/toolchain contract changes; no relative-cwd or producer-boundary claim. Canonical proof: docs/specs/trust/decision_trust-inventory.md, Absolute Cargo diagnostic-prefix proof (leaf M3.6.9.6.3.2.2.14.3.2.2.2.2.5).

from .any(|&(begin, end)| begin <= start && start < end)
to .any(|&(begin, end)| begin < start && start < end)
why On supported Unix Cargo-built callers, all raw paths are absolute from the guarded CLI/gate/inventory/compile chain; target resolution, successful canonicalization, ancestors, lossy conversion and apostrophe quoting preserve their leading slash. Every recorded prefix thus begins with slash. The edited comparison differs only at begin == start, but a candidate there begins with error and cannot simultaneously begin a slash-prefixed match. Every original containing span already has begin < start, so membership, selection and returned bytes agree for any stderr/environment with absolute cwd. This universal first-byte argument is independent of Cargo's diagnostic grammar; finite records only support it. Permanent exact production/caller guards, actual compiled helper/edit, independent literals/aliases/relative targets/line endings and generated records, native Cargo-root control, relative wider witness, altered-premise and wrong-oracle controls delimit the domain. Revalidate source/callers/root/constructors, prefix conversion, line/predicate or Unix/toolchain contracts; no arbitrary relative-cwd equivalence. Canonical proof: docs/specs/trust/decision_trust-inventory.md, Absolute Cargo diagnostic-prefix proof (leaf M3.6.9.6.3.2.2.14.3.2.2.2.2.5).


from (w[0] == "-C" && w[1].starts_with("extra-filename="))
to (w[0] == "-C" && w[1].starts_with("extra-filename"))
why For the current Unix inventory caller with pinned stable Cargo f2d3ce0bd7f24a49f8f72d9000448f8838c4e850 / Rust 1.95.0, every adjacent pair whose first token is -C either has no extra-filename prefix or has the complete ASCII extra-filename= constructor. Cargo emits the optional suffix as extra-filename=- plus a sixteen-hex UnitHash, or omits it. All other codegen constructors retain distinct initial keys for any value. Both role/test and generated-entry compile routes use fixed build or test/no-run commands without trailing compiler args; cleared allowlisted environment, reset Cargo homes and alias-only ancestor-checked config exclude arbitrary flags/wrappers, hard metadata preflight excludes dynamic package code independently of manifest admissions, and the pinned stable gate excludes profile rustflags. Source/name/type, lint/check-cfg, dependency and directory constructors cannot introduce a distinguishing incidental adjacent pair; in particular arbitrary custom check-cfg values are followed by fixed option tokens, not arbitrary suffix operands. The observer forwards immutable native argv and the consumer selects only successful current compilation records after Cargo succeeds. Thus both predicates choose the same first pair or the same empty default; the unchanged fifteen-byte slice starts after the same complete ASCII prefix at a valid UTF-8 boundary and returns identical bytes, preserving dep-info selection and subsequent behavior. Permanent exact production/controller/observer/base/configuration/metadata/parser/tree/module/dependency/pin guards outside semantic tests, actual compiled original/edit, complete real ordinary/incremental/mixed argv and three consumed libraries, literal/constructor/adjacency controls, wider changed-output and short/Unicode panic witnesses, nineteen altered-premise controls and three wrong-oracle controls delimit the proof. Wider argv is explicitly not equivalent; finite producer agreement is not the proof. This conditional lemma covers actual successful invocations by that pinned producer; other judged-tree toolchain producers are outside it. Revalidate producer/pin, both callers, environment/config/admissions/preflight, transitive readers/module/dependency wiring, constructors/adjacency, record filter or extraction/slicing changes. Canonical proof: docs/specs/trust/compiler-provenance-contract.md, Caller dep-info suffix prefix proof; full source argument: docs/book/src/annex-trust-proofs.md#caller-dep-info-suffix-prefix-proof-after-preflight-repair (leaf M3.6.9.6.3.2.2.15.2.1.4.3.1).
